    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1952-p28.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The successive differences of the \\(y\\)-values are \\(4,6,8,10,\\) whose successive differences are all \\(2.\\) Thus the data fit a monic quadratic. Substitution shows \\[ y=x^2+x+1 \\] gives \\(3,7,13,21,31\\) at \\(x=1,2,3,4,5,\\) respectively.\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Look at the first and second differences of the \\(y\\)-values",
        "The constant second difference \\(2\\) suggests a monic quadratic; test the listed quadratic"
      ],
